Which runtime for which build, and why
--------------------------------------
Rule: the runtime (msvcp140.dll etc.) must be the same or newer than the toolset that built the DLLs,
and it must itself run on the target OS. A newer runtime runs older-built DLLs (MS keeps v14 backward
compatible since VS2015); the reverse is not guaranteed. The breaking changes that set the limits:

1. 2020, after VS2019 16.7 (14.27): the v14 runtime officially drops Windows XP.
   Last XP-capable redistributable: 14.27.29114.0 (some report 14.28.29213.0 still working).
   XP builds need v141_xp, /Zc:threadSafeInit-, and this old runtime.
   See https://github.com/AviSynth/AviSynthPlus/issues/241

2. 2024, VS2022 17.10 (14.40): std::mutex got a constexpr constructor.
   A DLL built with 14.40 or newer, run on an older msvcp140.dll (before 14.40), crashes with an
   access violation at the first mutex lock. Microsoft calls it by design; see
   https://github.com/microsoft/STL/issues/4730
   Older DLLs on a newer runtime are fine. The AviSynth+ core uses std::mutex, so it is affected.
   Building with _DISABLE_CONSTEXPR_MUTEX_CONSTRUCTOR avoids it (the DLL then runs on old runtimes too).

3. 2025, VS2026 (14.50): the toolset and the runtime drop Windows 7, 8 and 8.1 (Win10 / Server 2016 minimum).
   The 14.50+ STL calls Windows 8+ APIs unconditionally. The latest redistributable (14.51 when last
   checked) does not run on Windows 7.
   The 14.44 line (VS2022 17.14, v143) is the last one for Windows 7: the Win7 build is made with
   the 14.44 toolset and ships the 14.44.35211.0 redistributable.
   Windows 7 SP1 / Server 2008 R2 also needs KB2999226 (Universal C Runtime).
   Reported working on Server 2008 R2 x64 (Doom9, 2026-02).

The build number within a minor line does not matter (14.44.35207 toolset with the 14.44.35211 runtime is fine).

Important note on XP
--------------------
  Microsoft ended support for Windows XP on April 8, 2014.
  XP-specific AviSynth builds still require a _compatible_ (= not latest) Visual C++ runtime.
  The last redistributable to support Windows XP is version 16.7 (file version 14.27.29114.0*).
  If Windows XP apps are deployed with or updated to a later version of the redistributable, the apps won't run.
  https://my.visualstudio.com/downloads?Visual%20Studio%202019%20version%2016.7

  *Others experienced that the latest XP compatible version is 14.28.29213.0.
  Links to official installers for last XP compatible Microsoft Visual C++ 2015-2019 Redistributable (version 14.28.29213):
  x64 - https://download.visualstudio.microsoft.com/download/pr/566435ac-4e1c-434b-b93f-aecc71e8cffc/B75590149FA14B37997C35724BC93776F67E08BFF9BD5A69FACBF41B3846D084/VC_redist.x64.exe
  x86 - https://download.visualstudio.microsoft.com/download/pr/566435ac-4e1c-434b-b93f-aecc71e8cffc/0D59EC7FDBF05DE813736BF875CEA5C894FFF4769F60E32E87BD48406BBF0A3A/VC_redist.x86.exe
